  "mimo": {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/pulls/2603",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/pull/2603",
    "body": "### Type of change\n\nBug fix / API addition\n\n### What does this PR do?\n\nEmbedded clients currently dispose directory instances to apply model or provider settings, which also discards unrelated conversation state and subscriptions. This PR adds `POST /global/provider/refresh` and `client.global.refreshProviders()` to update model configuration and provider caches while keeping those instances alive.\n\nRefresh admits work only when existing instances are idle, prepares every model view before publishing, and retains the prior views if preparation fails. HTTP handlers and server-initiated MCP sampling hold activity claims until completion. Cold configuration and plugin state stay uninitialized.\n\n### Explicit boundaries\n\n- `applied` means model settings were published. `pending` means busy: nothing is queued, and the caller must retry. Errors leave prior settings active.\n- MCP, skill, and plugin configuration changes still require an explicit restart. This PR adds no MCP registration or duplicate-name compatibility mechanism.\n- Existing authentication behavior is preserved. Refresh does not introduce per-request credential checks or immediate invalidation of previously obtained SDK objects.\n- No database migrations or Desktop changes are included. This PR remains a draft for human review.\n\n### How did you verify your code works?\n\n- Config, Provider, Instance, MCP, and HTTP regression tests: 1,006 passed, 4 skipped. MCP suites with module mocks ran in separate processes. Provider refresh suites also run separately because their process-wide idle precondition cannot inherit detached work from other suites; all 13 refresh tests pass.\n- After the final teardown admission fix, 110 affected regression tests passed.\n- Workspace/script typechecking and SDK compilation: passed.\n- Repository lint: 0 errors; warnings remain.\n- Node build and plain Node HTTP/SDK smoke: passed, including authorization, refresh, and the existing provider client.\n\nIndependent Compose Next review passed spec compliance, correctness, and codebase consistency with no unresolved findings.\n\nThe [feature document](docs/compose/spec/provider-local-refresh.md) records exact verification results and independent review evidence.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have tested my changes locally\n- [x] I have not included unrelated changes in this PR\n",
